<title>JAPAN: Japan's Kankaku says Wakabayashi to leave company.</title>
<headline>Japan's Kankaku says Wakabayashi to leave company.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Eishi Wakabayashi, vice president of the U.S. unit of Japan's Kankaku Securities Co Ltd, will leave the company on December 31 for personal reasons, a Kankaku spokesman in Tokyo said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Wakabayashi was a well-known figure in the foreign exchange market in Tokyo and accurately predicted that the dollar would fall to 80 yen last year, currency dealers said.</p>
<p>No more details were available.</p>
</text>
